              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Lalabee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It is critical to note that you DO NOT add the cola and milk in any order, you must add the cola prior to the milk or the carbonation will curdle the milk.\nIt is best to use a generic brand cola or to leave your \"coke\" open to the point where it is slightly flat.\nBar cola is rarely ever very fizzy and it is the reason it works well in the drink"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ugh Lee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I only add a splash of cola and add it at the very end. Then just stir with a straw. Basically a White Russian with a splash of cola. If using a glass as big as the one shown in the picture, definitely add more parts vodka and kahlua, after all it is called a “Paralyzer”! ??",
            "datePublished": "2021-08-03T09:30:22.820Z"
          },
